   "read_only": 1,
   "description": "When the retry ladder may begin. Starts at the due date, and is pushed forward whenever a collection attempt fails on our side — so a billing-run backlog never costs the customer their grace period."
  },
  {
   "fieldname": "period_key",
   "fieldtype": "Data",
   "label": "Period Key",
   "unique": 1,
   "read_only": 1,
   "hidden": 1,
   "no_copy": 1,
   "description": "Uniqueness key for 'one live invoice per (team, billing group, period)' — the constraint that makes double-billing impossible rather than merely unlikely (ADR 0018, invariant I6). Set from (team, billing_group, period_start, period_end) while the invoice is live, with an empty group segment for the team's consolidated invoice; replaced by a per-invoice sentinel on cancellation so a reissue can take the slot. Derived — never set it by hand."
  },
